        "id": "ex-qft-four-point-one-loop-log-degree",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "A four-point quartic one-loop graph has logarithmic superficial degree",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "prop-qft-four-dimensional-log-scale-anomaly",
          "prop-qft-quartic-superficial-degree"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "prop-qft-four-dimensional-log-scale-anomaly": "mathematical-premise",
          "prop-qft-quartic-superficial-degree": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "dependency_level": 5,
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Alexander M. Polyakov's QFT I course material, reconstructed and expanded by QFT.org, lesson 39: One-Loop Divergences and Power Counting",
              "url": "https://qft.org/courses/qft-i/39-one-loop-divergences-and-power-counting/"
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-posted prepublication draft, §§12 and 18",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf"
            }
          ]
        },
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "In Euclidean momentum dimension $D=4$, take the connected graph with two quartic vertices joined by two internal edges and with two external half-edges at each vertex. Its counts are $V=2$, $I=2$, $E=4$, and $L=1$. Its superficial degree is therefore zero, so it has logarithmic **superficial** degree under the stated power-counting convention.\n\nSeparately, on punctured Euclidean $\\mathbb R^4$ let $C_0(x)=1/(4\\pi^2|x|^2)$ and $u=C_0^2=1/(16\\pi^4|x|^4)$. For any $\\chi\\in\\mathcal D(\\mathbb R^4)$ equal to one near $0$, and every $\\mu>0$, define $T_\\mu(\\varphi)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^4\\setminus\\{0\\}}[\\varphi(x)-\\chi(\\mu x)\\varphi(0)]/(16\\pi^4|x|^4)\\,d^4x$ for $\\varphi\\in\\mathcal D(\\mathbb R^4)$. Conditional on the current QFT-IR04 proposition [[prop-qft-four-dimensional-log-scale-anomaly]] with its explicit Axiom-of-Choice hypothesis, this family has the exact logarithmic scale-change identity stated below and no same-degree homogeneous extension. This is a separate Euclidean distribution-extension calculation; it is not identified with the integrated amplitude of the graph. The graph count alone does not establish convergence or divergence of an actual loop integral."
      }
    ]
  }
]
